  "question_stem": "Chen has three boxes. Box $A$ contains 5 counters, of which 3 are white and 2 are yellow. Box $W$ contains 4 red marbles and 3 blue marbles. Box $Y$ contains 5 red marbles and 3 blue marbles.\n\nChen chooses one counter at random from box $A$. If the counter is white, he chooses two marbles from box $W$, at random and without replacement. If the counter is yellow, he chooses two marbles from box $Y$, at random and without replacement.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$P(W)=\\frac35$ and $P(Y)=\\frac25$; after $W$, the red/blue probabilities are $\\frac47,\\frac37$ followed by $\\frac36,\\frac36$ or $\\frac46,\\frac26$; after $Y$, they are $\\frac58,\\frac38$ followed by $\\frac47,\\frac37$ or $\\frac57,\\frac27$.",
    "$P(\\text{one red and one blue})=\\frac{39}{70}$."
  ],
